            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="0354" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg238"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/514.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1233.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-12-04">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">December</hi> 4, 1911</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my dispatch No. 1225 of
                    the 1st instant [etc.] I have the honor to report that a bill signed by Messrs.
                    Freyre Andrade, González Lanuza and other Conservative members has now been
                    introduced in the lower House of Congress to repeal in their entirety the civil
                    service law drafted by the late Provisional Government and the complementary and
                    promulgatory act of January 18, 1911.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh S. Gibson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
